Good morning!

Thank you all for responding to this request, and for uploading those files=
. However, I believe they are incomplete. One critical part of assessing el=
igibility is not only the date of the qualifying drought, but also the type=
 of qualifying drought.

Specifically, FSA Guidance document 1-LFP Amendment 6 (https://www.fsa.usda=
.gov/Internet/FSA_File/1lfp-a6.pdf) Paragraph 23B indicates, =93The Nationa=
l Office will notify State and County Offices eligible for LFP by posting a=
 list of eligible counties by pasture type every Thursday at [https://usdag=
cc.sharepoint.com/sites/FPAC-FSA-FPAC-FSA-LFPStateProgramSpecialists/LFP%20=
Eligibility%20Reports/Forms/AllItems.aspx] under "LFP Eligible Counties=94.=
=94 The LFP Eligible Counties Report contains the following columns:


  *
State
  *
County
  *
Program Year
  *
Pasture Type
  *
D2 Qualifying Drought Start and End Dates (duration of 8 consecutive weeks)
  *
D3a Qualifying Drought Start and End Dates (duration of 1 day)
  *
D3b Qualifying Drought Start and End Dates (duration of 4 non-consecutive w=
eeks)
  *
D4a Qualifying Drought Start and End Dates (duration of 1 day)
  *
D4b Qualifying Drought Start and End Dates (duration of 4 non-consecutive w=
eeks)
  *
Date of Qualifying Drought
  *
Drought Factor
  *
Grazing Period Start and End Dates
  *
Maximum Eligible Payment Months
  *
Payment Factor.

Among the files you uploaded, only the 2009=962011 file included start and =
end dates for D2, D3a, D3b, and D4 qualifying droughts (it didn=92t split D=
4a and D4b, but it should have). Were you able to find those data for all t=
he other years? They are essential for the analysis I=92m doing with suppor=
t from the USDA OCE.

Thank you!

Best,
Kyle


Kyle Bocinsky, PhD

Director of Climate Extension, Montana Climate Office, University of Montan=
a<https://climate.umt.edu/>
Asst. Research Professor, Society and Conservation, University of Montana<h=
ttps://www.umt.edu/environment/about/departments/socon/default.php>

The University of Montana acknowledges that we are in the aboriginal territ=
ories of the Salish and Kalispel people. We honor the path they have shown =
us in caring for this place for the generations to come.

